From e056695c3473bee7ac5d90011a4c95c6b83d275b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 00:35:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Move the Monte Carlo constants into one file

gen_montecarlo.m and sweep_nonneg.m each carried their own copy of what the
experiment is -- LMAX_FIT/LMAX_GT, CS_phase, KAPPA, ANGLES, K_WM, the fibre
axis, the RNG seed -- plus their own copies of pick_grid, divisors_of and
rotate_about. Two definitions of one experiment is how the sweep and the main
run drift apart without anyone noticing.

mc_config.m is now the single definition. Both scripts read from it, and the
duplicated local functions are gone. condition_axes(ic) replaces the if/else
that built the fibre axes in both files, so the crossing geometry is defined
once. The constants are documented where they are defined rather than in
whichever script the reader happens to open first.

Behaviour is unchanged, and that is checked rather than assumed: both scripts
were run before and after at SNR 30 with 8 reps per condition, and every
output is byte-for-byte identical -- 18 files for gen_montecarlo.m (including
the fitted kernel and the SMI fODF coefficients) and 19 for sweep_nonneg.m
(including all six regularizer settings). The seeds keep their values, so the
noise realisations are the same ones the report's numbers came from.

